    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cebbe49e_2a7f54ec",
        "filename": "acme/errors.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-04-04T22:25:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Things named starting with \"Err\" are conventionally values of type \"error\", not string.\n\n(Likewise, things named ending in \"Error\" are error _types_)\n\nSo I wonder if these should be of some error type so they implement error. Or maybe they don\u0027t need to be exported.",
      "revId": "0ac8ab9e8a840bae1a02a0b5d769323cf59c03be",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ec48060_f8432d12",
        "filename": "acme/errors.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-04-06T11:41:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, agree, the \"Err\" convention bothers me as well.\n\nWe have Error which implements error, but it has Status and Detail which can be arbitrary values, not consts.\n\nIt seems making these implement error would gain little value since it\u0027s just partial error information, the rest is in Status and Detail.\n\nMaybe we could do something like this:\n\n  type BadCSRError struct {\n    Error\n  }\n\n  func (e *BadCSRError) Type() string {\n    return \"urn:acme:error:badCSR\"\n  }\n\nand the same for all other known errors. That is, have Type() method, not a field. WDYT?\n\nIn any event, go/certs-bridge uses these to handle errors. We need to surface it somehow.",
      "parentUuid": "cebbe49e_2a7f54ec",
      "revId": "0ac8ab9e8a840bae1a02a0b5d769323cf59c03be",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b06ce0a_9c0a4541",
        "filename": "acme/errors.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-04-09T15:16:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Or we could just rename these to ProblemXxx. It\u0027s what they call it in http://tools.ietf.org/html/draft-ietf-appsawg-http-problem.\n\n  ProblemBadCSR   \u003d \"urn:acme:error:badCSR\"\n  ProblemBadNonce \u003d \"...\"\n  ...",
      "parentUuid": "2ec48060_f8432d12",
      "revId": "0ac8ab9e8a840bae1a02a0b5d769323cf59c03be",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6b24aaf3_878d86f6",
        "filename": "acme/errors.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 6347
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-04-12T13:39:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ok, so I\u0027ve just checked internal usage and turns out ErrXxx constants are not in use anymore: Error.Status + Error.Header is sufficient.\n\nRemoving ErrXxx for now. We can always come back to this in the future if needed.",
      "parentUuid": "0b06ce0a_9c0a4541",
      "revId": "0ac8ab9e8a840bae1a02a0b5d769323cf59c03be",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8b3abef4_7a445999",
        "filename": "acme/errors.go",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 16,
      "author": {
        "id": 5065
      },
      "writtenOn": "2016-04-12T15:39:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sounds good. I like \"problem\". It\u0027s fortunate for us that the spec calls them that, giving us justification in using that term.",
      "parentUuid": "6b24aaf3_878d86f6",
      "revId": "0ac8ab9e8a840bae1a02a0b5d769323cf59c03be",
      "serverId": "62eb7196-b449-3ce5-99f1-c037f21e1705",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
